    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded around 1528 by a son of the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a> claimed Malacca's royal line and maritime empire.</li><li>It allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> in 1641 and became the leading Malay <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepôt</a> of the late seventeenth century.</li><li>Its partition by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> in 1824 created modern borders; it survives as a monarchy within Malaysia.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a>'s constitution of 1895, issued under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-bakar-of-johor">Sultan Abu Bakar</a>, forbade any ruler from surrendering the state or any part of it to a foreign power.</p></aside>
    </section>

