ef="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-shah-ii-of-johor">Mahmud Shah II</a> is murdered, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> line</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1819</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stamford-raffles">Raffles</a> recognises Hussein as sultan and founds British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1824</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-dutch-treaty-of-1824">Anglo-Dutch Treaty</a> splits the realm; Riau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lingga-islands">Lingga</a> goes to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> sphere</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1885</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> recognises <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-bakar-of-johor">Abu Bakar</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2024</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibrahim-iskandar-of-johor">Ibrahim Iskandar</a> becomes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-di-pertuan-agong">King of Malaysia</a></span></li></ol>
